  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "Cómo te mueves",
    "@en": "How you move"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "El medio de transporte se dice con **by**: **by bus**, **by train**, **by car**, **by bike**. Pero «a pie» es **on foot**.",
     "@en": "The means of transport is said with **by**: **by bus**, **by train**, **by car**, **by bike**. But «a pie» is **on foot**."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**How do you get to work?** = ¿cómo vas al trabajo?",
     "@en": "**How do you get to work?** = how are you going to work?"
    },
    {
     "@es": "Para decir cuánto se tarda: **It takes twenty minutes** (se tarda veinte minutos). **How long does it take?** = ¿cuánto se tarda?",
     "@en": "To say how long it takes: **It takes twenty minutes** (it takes 20 minutes). **How long does it take?** = how long does it take?"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": {
    "@es": "En la estación",
    "@en": "At the station"
   },
   "texto": [
    {
     "@es": "**A ticket to Oxford, please** (un billete para Oxford).",
     "@en": "**A ticket to Oxford, please** (a ticket to Oxford)."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**Single** = solo ida. **Return** = ida y vuelta.",
     "@en": "**Single** = one-way. **Return** = back and forth."
    },
    {
     "@es": "**What time does the train leave?** (¿a qué hora sale el tren?). El tren sale de un **platform** (andén).",
     "@en": "**What time does the train leave?** (what time does the train leave?). The train leaves a **platform** (platform)."
    }
   ]
